    "narrative": "LawDog\u2019s optimal lineup for July 4th leans heavily into exploitative matchups against vulnerable arms, with **Lawrence Butler** (73.47) and **Tyler Freeman** (71.80) emerging as our top-tier plays. **Lawrence Butler** benefits from a prime #3 spot against Sandy Alcantara, where a combination of a hitter-friendly park and a favorable platoon advantage drives his high efficiency. Similarly, **Tyler Freeman** is positioned for a breakout performance; despite the left-on-left dynamic against Robbie Ray, the park factors and the underlying projection strength make him a core contributor. **Luis Arraez** also carries a strong 66.78, capitalizing on the high-xERA mark of Sean Sullivan to solidify his role at the top of the order, providing the necessary floor for our AVG category.\n\nOur most difficult roster construction choice involved the exclusion of **Gavin Sheets**, whose 45.19 score left him just outside the threshold for a start. While he projects as a capable utility bat, the optimizer penalized him for the difficult matchup against Yoshinobu Yamamoto, favoring the higher-ceiling profiles of **Masyn Winn** and **Daulton Varsho** despite their own situational hurdles. Meanwhile, we remain wary of the rain risk (42%) surrounding the games involving **Dylan Beavers** and **Taylor Ward**, which heavily influenced their relegation to the bench in favor of more stable, dry-weather options. We are monitoring the pending lineups for **Jonathan Aranda**, **Geraldo Perdomo**, **Bryson Stott**, **Drew Gilbert**, **Jung Hoo Lee**, and **Masyn Winn** closely; should any of these players move down in their respective batting orders, their daily efficiency scores will require immediate re-evaluation. While **Cal Raleigh** faces the formidable Bieber, his strong underlying metrics and high-leverage lineup slot maintain his position as a confident start.",
